  "hints": [
    "Rotating by a multiple of len(items) brings the list back to its original order, so reduce k using k % len(items).",
    "Python negative slicing items[-r:] + items[:-r] constructs a new rotated list cleanly when r = k % len(items) and r > 0.",
    "Pseudocode:\n  if not items: return []\n  r = k % len(items)\n  return items[-r:] + items[:-r] if r else list(items)"
